{"id":"b744279d55b870f3","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-binary-np-completeness-transfer.md","title":"NP-Completeness Transfers Along Polynomial Many-One Reductions","display":"thm-np-completeness-upward — NP-Completeness Transfers Along Polynomial Many-One Reductions","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-binary-np-completeness-transfer","aliases":["73-thm-binary-np-completeness-transfer","73-thm-np-completeness-upward"],"display":"thm-np-completeness-upward — NP-Completeness Transfers Along Polynomial Many-One Reductions","depends_on":["[[73-df-binary-np]]","[[73-df-binary-np-completeness]]","[[73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-binary-np-completeness-transfer"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-binary-np-completeness-transfer</span><span>73-thm-np-completeness-upward</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-np-completeness-upward — NP-Completeness Transfers Along Polynomial Many-One Reductions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ebe5483ba604bc90\" href=\"?note=ebe5483ba604bc90\" title=\"73-df-binary-np\">73-df-binary-np</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"41d5b79d11297576\" href=\"?note=41d5b79d11297576\" title=\"73-df-binary-np-completeness\">73-df-binary-np-completeness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"69f4f24da36d1d66\" href=\"?note=69f4f24da36d1d66\" title=\"73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one\">73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{NP}\">\\(\\mathsf{NP}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{NPC}\">\\(\\mathsf{NPC}\\)</span> (NP and its complete languages)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m^p\">\\(\\leq_m^p\\)</span> (polynomial-time many-one reducibility, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"69f4f24da36d1d66\" href=\"?note=69f4f24da36d1d66\" title=\"73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one\">73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}np\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}upward}\\vdash\n\\forall L,L&#39;\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\\Bigl(\nL\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\\land L\\leq_m^p L&#39;\\land L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NP}\n\\longrightarrow L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}np\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}upward}\\vdash\n\\forall L,L&#39;\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\\Bigl(\nL\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\\land L\\leq_m^p L&#39;\\land L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NP}\n\\longrightarrow L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathsf{NP}\">\\(A\\in\\mathsf{NP}\\)</span>, completeness gives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\leq_m^pL\">\\(A\\leq_m^pL\\)</span>. Composing its polynomial-time witness with the witness for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\leq_m^pL&#39;\">\\(L\\leq_m^pL&#39;\\)</span> gives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\leq_m^pL&#39;\">\\(A\\leq_m^pL&#39;\\)</span>; polynomial output length follows from the running-time bound. The explicit premise <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NP}\">\\(L&#39;\\in\\mathsf{NP}\\)</span> supplies the remaining half of NP-completeness.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-np","status":"resolved","id":"ebe5483ba604bc90","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-np]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-np-completeness","status":"resolved","id":"41d5b79d11297576","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-np-completeness]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one","status":"resolved","id":"69f4f24da36d1d66","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one","status":"resolved","id":"69f4f24da36d1d66","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\leq_m^p$ (polynomial-time many-one reducibility, see [[73-df-binary-polynomial-many-one]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathsf{NP}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{NPC}","display":false},{"tex":"\\leq_m^p","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}np\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}upward}\\vdash\n\\forall L,L'\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\\Bigl(\nL\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\\land L\\leq_m^p L'\\land L'\\in\\mathsf{NP}\n\\longrightarrow L'\\in\\mathsf{NPC}\n\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"A\\in\\mathsf{NP}","display":false},{"tex":"A\\leq_m^pL","display":false},{"tex":"L\\leq_m^pL'","display":false},{"tex":"A\\leq_m^pL'","display":false},{"tex":"L'\\in\\mathsf{NP}","display":false}],"bytes":1274,"backlinks":[{"id":"643ca49e5f5f7846","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["ebe5483ba604bc90","41d5b79d11297576","69f4f24da36d1d66"]}